## 4. NORTHSTAR 1.1 Core principles

### 4.1 Early static verification
Claim: contracts, bounds, types, and caps check at compile time.
Lock: `../ooda/scripts/contracts_native_smoke.oo`, `typecheck_pass_smoke.oo`, `json_errors_smoke.oo`.
Exists? yes. Production? yes (const header fold). Full SMT is 5.1 residual. Open? no.

### 4.2 Zero ambient authority
Claim: no implicit fs, net, process, or hardware access.
Lock: `../ooda/scripts/hostile_cap_probe_smoke.oo`, `objcap_landlock_smoke.oo`, `open_rlimit_smoke.oo`.
Exists? yes. Production? yes. Open? no.

### 4.3 Deterministic execution
Claim: bit-identical compile, zero-timestamp digests, reproducible binaries.
Lock: `../ooda/scripts/bit_identical_emit_lock.oo` (emit-c, emit-llvm, emit-wasm).
Exists? yes. Production? emit identity yes. Raw gcc `cmp` is 5.3. Full binary identity is a moonshot. Open? no.

### 4.4 Agent-native tooling
Claim: JSON diagnostics, AST reflection, `ooda fix` / `ooda patch`.
Lock: `json_errors_smoke.oo`, `outline_reflect_smoke.oo`, `emust_autofix_smoke.oo`, `patch_smoke.oo`, `lsp_cursor_smoke.oo`.
Exists? yes. Production? yes. vscode `ooda-lsp.js` is 5.1 residual. Open? no.

### 4.5 High performance
Claim: zero-overhead, cache-coherent layouts, native codegen.
Lock: `../ooda/scripts/ci_open_run.oo`, `c_emit_smoke.oo`, `dod_soa_smoke.oo`, `open60_92_prove.oo` (OPEN-85).
Exists? yes. Production? native C emit yes. Auto-emit SoA is a moonshot. Open? no.

## 5. NORTHSTAR 4.2 Static capability verification

### 5.1 Unforgeable tokens
Claim: FsRead/Write, Net, Tcp, Udp, Sys, Process, Env, Time, Rand, Alloc, Thread, Gpu, Ffi.
Lock: `caps_matrix_smoke.oo`, `caps_product_floor_smoke.oo`, `hostile_cap_probe_smoke.oo`, `alloc_cap_smoke.oo`, `cap_dns_udp_smoke.oo`.
Exists? yes. Production? yes. Open? no.

### 5.2 Borrowed capabilities
Claim: `&Cap` exercises an effect without ownership.
Lock: every named smoke and `../qa/identity_lock.oo` (formal `&FsReadCap`).
Exists? yes. Production? yes. Open? no.

### 5.3 Attenuation
Claim: holders derive a narrower token.
Lock: `../ooda/scripts/hostile_cap_probe_smoke.oo` (forged parent differs).
Exists? yes. Production? yes. Open? no.

### 5.4 Default-deny E_CAP
Claim: a privileged call without a token fails closed at check time.
Lock: `json_errors_smoke.oo`, `ecap_autofix_smoke.oo`, `emust_autofix_smoke.oo`, `../qa/qa_master.oo` trap phases.
Exists? yes. Production? yes. Open? no.

## 6. NORTHSTAR 4.5 SECRET taint

### 6.1 SECRET tags
Claim: `SECRET:` marks sensitive data.
Lock: `../ooda/scripts/secret_sink_enforce_smoke.oo`, `secret_product_floor_smoke.oo`.
Exists? yes. Production? yes. Open? no.

### 6.2 Taint through assign, pack, and call
Claim: taint follows assignment, struct fields, and calls.
Lock: `secret_t1_return_smoke.oo`, `secret_t2_depth_smoke.oo`.
Exists? yes. Production? yes (IDENT / field / call rails). Open? no.

### 6.3 Block unsealed sinks
Claim: tainted values cannot reach `process_exec`, open I/O, or untrusted FFI.
Lock: `secret_sink_enforce_smoke.oo` (println, write_file, fetch, sys_exec, process_exec, env_get, read_file, process_exit).
Exists? yes. Production? yes for those sinks. Open? no.

## 7. NORTHSTAR 5.1 Backend hierarchy

### 7.1 Floor native C emit
Claim: portable C plus `chs_rt`, then host gcc or clang.
Lock: `../ooda/scripts/ci_open_run.oo`, `c_emit_smoke.oo`, `ooda_run_product_smoke.oo`.
Exists? yes. Production? yes. This is the product path. Open? no.

### 7.2 LLVM emit
Claim: direct LLVM IR, SIMD, cross-module LTO.
Lock: `../ooda/scripts/open30_llvm_lock_smoke.oo`, `open68_stamp_smoke.oo`.
Exists? yes. Production? hello and stamp-walk yes. gcc replacement is 5.3. Open? no.

### 7.3 WASM target
Claim: sandboxed WebAssembly with zero ambient host caps.
Lock: `wasm_emit_smoke.oo`, `open_wasm_binary_smoke.oo`, `wasm_caps_smoke.oo`.
Exists? yes. Production? `\0asm` emit yes. Browser host and cap lowering stay residual. Open? no.

### 7.4 GPU / NPU kernels
Claim: compute dispatch behind `GpuCap`.
Lock: `open60_92_prove.oo` (OPEN-91 `emit_ptx`), `gpu_path_a_smoke.oo` (noop / cpu / device residual).
Exists? yes. Production? PTX text and fail-closed GpuCap yes. Device launch is 5.1 residual. Open? no.

### 7.5 Bare-metal freestanding
Claim: minimal runtime for embedded and microkernels.
Lock: `open60_92_prove.oo` (OPEN-92 `bare_metal_init`).
Exists? yes. Production? hosted canary yes. Pure `.oo` microkernel is a moonshot. Open? no.

## 8. Verdict

Every NORTHSTAR 1.1, 4.2, 4.5, and 5.1 production claim has at least one named lock.
No SHIPPED Lock path is missing.
Do not add a QA-suite growth row.
Do not add 5.3, 5.4, 5.1 residual, or moonshot work as this-cycle leftover.
C emit + gcc remains the product.

